      },
      "worked": "At $x=0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}2^{3(0)+1}&=k\\times3^{a(0)}\\\\2&=k\\end{align*}$$\nUsing index laws,\n$$\\begin{align*}2^{3x+1}&=2\\times(2^3)^x\\\\2^{3x+1}&=2\\times8^x\\end{align*}$$\nThus $8^x=3^{ax}$. At $x=1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}3^a&=8\\\\a&=\\log_3(8)\\end{align*}$$\nHence $k=2$ and $a=\\log_3(8)$. These values give $k\\times3^{ax}=2\\times(3^a)^x=2\\times8^x$, as required.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
